<LegalLayout title="Safety Center">
  <p class="lede">
    Placeholder structure for Pynapli's Safety Center. Safety is core to how Pynapli works — you
    stay in control of what’s seen, who reaches you, and how much you share.
  </p>

  <h2>Verification</h2>
  <p>Verify your profile so others know you’re real, and look for verified members.</p>

  <h2>Private albums</h2>
  <p>Your private photos are yours. They’re shared only when you choose — never automatically.</p>

  <h2>Blocking &amp; hiding</h2>
  <p>Block or hide anyone, anytime. Blocked members can’t see you or reach you.</p>

  <h2>Location privacy</h2>
  <p>Discovery uses your approximate area. Your exact location is never shown.</p>

  <h2>Meeting safely</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Chat first and trust your instincts.</li>
    <li>Meet in public the first time; tell a friend your plans.</li>
    <li>Look after your own transport and exit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reporting</h2>
  <p>Report profiles or messages that break our <a href="/guidelines">Community Guidelines</a>.</p>

  <h2>Get help</h2>
  <p><a href="mailto:safety@pynapli.com">safety@pynapli.com</a></p>
</LegalLayout>
